  4. dnoise recoverPoint (E): mzToTof(mz) where mz = loader's m/z of real peaks ≤ ~1700 real, or corrupt. mz up to whatever the loader wrote — if loader wrote m/z 4e4 (store cap), within domain. Actually recoverPoint gets s[i].getMZ() — any double from the loader. mz > m_vertex → mzToTof returns a small t → could accidentally round to a valid bin within kTofTol?? Then recoverPoint would identify the point as a different TOF bin than it was! Non-monotonic inverse: mz beyond vertex maps back to small t. If |t - bin| ≤ kTofTol (1e-6? kTofTol mentioned "recover::kTofTol" = 1e-6 bins) and the scan/im match, it returns Refusal::none with the WRONG tof. Then downstream the denoiser treats it as that bin — silently wrong m/z assignment? Wait, but the denoiser then re-converts bin → m/z with tofToMz and the output m/z would be the rising-branch m/z of that bin, not the original. The point of recoverPoint is to verify loader m/z == model m/z of the bin. If loader m/z is beyond-vertex, mzToTof gives t_small, bin = round(t_small), and the check passes only if the loader's m/z equals tofToMz(bin) — no wait, recoverPoint doesn't re-verify; it assumes mzToTof is the inverse. The check is |t - bin| ≤ tol. For an arbitrary mz, t = mzToTof(mz) lands within 1e-6 of an integer only if mz ≈ tofToMz(bin) — on the FALLING branch, tofToMz(bin) gives the rising-branch m/z, which differs from mz (falling branch m/z). Hmm, so would |mzToTof(mz) - bin| ≤ 1e-6 hold for mz = falling-branch m/z of bin b'? mzToTof(mz) with mz = t-value beyond vertex: mzToTof is closed-form t(mz) = C0 + b·sqrt(mz+C4) + C2(mz+C4). For mz on the falling branch image... the falling branch never happens in forward conversion: tofToMz only produces rising-branch m/z. The loader converts real bins via tofToMz — always rising branch. So mz values seen are rising-branch m/z of real bins, and mzToTof inverts them correctly (rising branch inverse, monotonic region since bins ≤ 4.3e9... hmm bins up to 2^32; for PXD, rising branch holds to 5.7e9 slope-half and 7.6e9 vertex-tof... vertex t = C0 + b²/k = tof 7.6e9 > 2^32 ✓ so all uint32 bins are pre-vertex for PXD). For a near-edge accepted calibration, vertex tof = 1.33e8 (4/3 × 1e8), bins above that don't exist in real files (N ≤ 1e8 < vertex tof). Corrupt blob bins up to 4.3e9 > vertex: tofToMz returns NaN for t > t_zero (1.33e8·...). NaN → recoverPoint refuses → tool throws. Fail closed ✓.

