  Findings list:

  **Findings:**

  F1 (Q4/Q3, MEDIUM, theoretical): OpenMS loader patch converts frames without frameReason — corrupt Frames.T1 (e.g. 1100 °C or -1e6 °C) on a negative-C2 file converts with unchecked C1 factor when the tool runs with -dnoise:ms1 false and the OpenMS detector (no loadTdfCalibration in that path). Before 1.3.1 such files were refused outright; now they're accepted and converted at an unverified temperature. Concrete: PXD1418's row with dC1 = 20 and a frame T1 = -973 °C (= T1_ref - 1000.6, outside span): cf = 1.0199... small error. To get large error need larger dC1: row with dC1 = 999 ppm/K (passes cf_lo > 0 barely: cf_lo = 0.001 > 0), T1 = T1_ref - 2000 K → cf = 2.998 → m/z off by factor ~3. MS1 spectra finite-positive → requireFiniteMs1Mz passes → silent wrong masses in MS1 map (MS2 compactify drops m/z > 42000 as bad_mz). Theoretical (corrupt file required), but it is a posture regression for exactly the newly-accepted class. Header lines 34-37 disclose it.

  F2 (Q8, MEDIUM process): CHANGELOG asserts "the four pins reproduce" before the digest gate ran. By-construction argument verified sound (see Q5), but the claim is stated as fact pre-verification.

  F3 (Q3, LOW, theoretical): The OpenMS loader converts unbounded uint32 TOF indices (patch F:182-185); the 1e8 domain is enforced only by loadTdfAxisBounds, which runs only in the integer-detector/mzPeak paths. For PXD-like calibrations the margin holds even at 2^32-1 (disc/b² = 0.437, section 3b), but for a hypothetical accepted near-edge calibration (|C2| = 0.0595), blob indices ≥ ~1.33e8 (beyond vertex) yield NaN m/z; with dnoise off these are dropped (MS2: bad_mz at diaspextract.cpp:730) or refused (MS1: requireFiniteMs1Mz at 3522) — fail-safe. Requires corrupt blob. LOW.

  F4 (Q3, LOW, theoretical): near-edge accepted calibrations: mzOf(n_bins-1) can exceed kDomainMaxMz (≈1.1e8 m/z for |C2|=0.0595), so tofOf(mzOf(last)+1e-5) at diaspextract.cpp:4116 inverts outside the verified m/z domain — still correct because monotonicity holds to the vertex (4× the half-slope mass), not because of the check. No wrong output; the "domain covers everything the tool asks" claim (header line 29-31) is slightly overstated on the m/z side.

  F5 (Q6, LOW): generator pins sha256 only for 1418/1420/1422 (KNOWN dict); 1431/1408/1347 unpinned. Provenance gap, easily fixed.

  F6 (Q6, LOW): golden JSON has no C4 key and neither parser reads it (test_calibration_cpp.cpp:80-88 parses 8 keys, C4 default-0; Python p.get("C4", 0.0)). A future golden file with C4 ≠ 0 would be silently tested at C4 = 0. Latent trap, not a current bug.

  F7 (Q6, LOW): per-file guards cover C2-ablation and sign-flip but not temperature; run 1347's temp ablation is 0.0776 ppm < the 0.1 global threshold, which passes only via dataset D's 0.669 ppm. A regenerated JSON with zero T1 spread on the new files would still pass. Weak but the global guard does its job today.

  F8 (Q8, LOW): CHANGELOG "On PXD029836 the discriminant is at least 0.984 b²" over all six runs — section 3b measures only the 1418/1420/1422 vector directly (0.98687); the 0.9845 for 1431's vector is extrapolation. True, but the evidence shown doesn't directly cover three of the four vectors at the 1e8/±1000 K corner.

  F9 (Q7, trivial): TdfLoad.h:57 refusal message hardcodes "[2, 1e8]" though the bound is now kDomainMaxTof — goes stale if the constant changes.

  Also Q5 mixed deploy: layout unchanged (static members/functions don't affect layout; no aggregate init anywhere — confirmed no `TdfMzCalibration{` uses); old libOpenMS + new tool: TdfLoad.h includes <OpenMS/FORMAT/TdfMzCalibration.h> — building the tool against an old installed header fails to compile (frameReason missing) — loud, fail-safe ✓. New libOpenMS + old tool: header identical logic superset; old tool doesn't call frameReason — fine. Also C++20 required (CMakeLists:11) → static constexpr fine.

  Wait — actually check: does diaspextract.cpp compile against the OpenMS-installed header or src? CMakeLists:50 configures a shim copying src/TdfMzCalibration.h to build dir OpenMS/FORMAT/. So the standalone build shims it — meaning the tool always compiles against its own src copy via the shim? "configure_file(src/TdfMzCalibration.h ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/shim/OpenMS/FORMAT/TdfMzCalibration.h COPYONLY)" — so TdfLoad.h's <OpenMS/FORMAT/TdfMzCalibration.h> resolves to the shim copy first (if include order puts shim first). That neutralizes the mixed-deploy compile issue for the standalone CMake build; for the in-tree TOPP build (sync_cluster), dest() installs the header into the OpenMS tree and builds both together (line 102 grep ensures the patch is applied, 118 installs header). So mixed deploy is guarded by the deploy transaction + provenance sha (test_sync_cluster_txn.sh:122,128 check header sha equality). Nice — mention in Q5 that the sha-pinned deploy transaction guards this; remaining risk is a hand-built deploy, fail-safe direction.

  Q1 answer: derivation. Both roots positive for C0 < t < C0 + b²/(4|C2|)? Roots: u_± = (b ∓ sqrt(disc))/(2|C2|), disc ∈ [0, b²) for t in (C0, t_vertex): sqrt(disc) ∈ [0, b] → u_+ ∈ [0, b/(2|C2|)] ≥ 0, u_- ∈ [b/(2|C2|), b/|C2|] > 0. Yes both positive (u_+ = 0 at t = C0). Code's form = u_+ rationalized = rising branch ✓. No t or b returns the other root: denominator b + sqrt(disc) > 0 always; numerator ≥ 0 with t > C0 guard. Continuity through C2 = 0: limit (t-C0)/b ✓; at C2 = -0.0 bit-identical ✓ (IEEE: b² - (±0) = b²).

  Hmm, one edge at the vertex t = t_vertex exactly: disc = 0, u = 2(t-C0)/(2b) = (t-C0)/b = b/(2|C2|) = u_v — correct double root. ✓

  Q2: t_zero, t_half, u_half verified by derivation above. Deciding corner verified: disc = b² - k(t - C0), decreasing in t and increasing in b²; min over domain at max t, min b; b min at max C1 factor = cf_hi via fabs(dC1) — both signs ✓. m/z condition: mz + C4 ≤ u_half² for all mz ≤ 1e5 ⟺ 1e5 + C4 ≤ u_half² ✓; negative C4 loosens correctly, positive tightens ✓; u_half² overflow → +inf → condition true — but then t-side: t_half = inf → accepted; check what that means: k tiny → vertex at astronomically large u — genuinely safe ✓. Accepted-while-violating row: none found; proof: for any T1 in span, b(T1) ≥ b_check (up to 1-ulp FP, immaterial vs 0.25 threshold); for any tof ≤ 1e8: t ≤ t_max ≤ t_half(b_check) ≤ t_half(b(T1)) → disc ≥ b²/4. Message garbage: only if digitizer_timebase denormal (division → inf prints "inf") or delay ±inf — refused either way, message cosmetic. LOW/theoretical.

  Note the subtle pre-existing gap the fix inherits: unsupportedReason screens NaN but not ±inf for timebase/delay/C0 (line 76). For C2 < 0, inf timebase/delay lead to refusal or all-NaN conversions — fail-safe. Unchanged for C2 ≥ 0. Not a new finding, mention in passing.

  Q4: also floating-point comparison consistency: frameReason admits |ΔT| ≤ 1000 inclusive; domain cf_hi computed as 1 + |dC1|·1000/1e6 — same op order as frameFactor at exactly ΔT = ±1000 → identical rounding ✓. 1000 K sensible: real spans ≤ 0.034 K; cf_lo guard refuses |dC1| ≥ 1000 ppm/K with negative C2 (real dC1 = 20) ✓ never refuses a real file.

